Z||000005||TRiAD||10-24-2001||01:12 AM||||Nice selections...<P>Of the cars listed, I'd suggest the following...(no particular order)<P>1) 300ZX Turbo. VERY nice car, but they are all going south quick. Apparently these had a 10 year lifespan, at best. Parts are PHENOMINALLY expensive, and nice ones are getting harder to find, and more expensive. <P>2) 300ZX NA. Basically a Japanese Camaro (or what the Japanese thought the Camaro SHOULD have been). Much nicer these days than the turbos, and cheaper, you can get a 2+2 (insurance) and they have 222HP from the factory. <P>3) MR2T (actually 0-60 was 6.0 flat). Nice, if you can find a clean one. Like the ZTT, I'd avoid aftermarket modded cars like the plague. I would also recommend the NA MR2 before the T. The turbos in both of these cars will run you BIG $$ to replace (and they WILL need replaced). <P>Best of luck in your search. I would also suggest you look into the 3rd gen RX7. They're getting cheaper, and $3K in the bank will get you a WHOLE NEW ENGINE...INSTALLED...whenever you need it. (about every 50-80Kmi). <P>Keep us posted!<P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg"> <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||1
